/P 244 0 R
/E (The chart illustrates the parabolic trajectory of the U.S. Federal Debt, which has surged from approximately $5.7 trillion in 2000 to nearly $40 trillion by early 2026. This visualization highlights several critical inflection points, most notably the 2008 financial crisis and the 2020 pandemic response, both of which catalyzed structural shifts in fiscal policy and accelerated the deficit. The increasingly steep slope in recent years underscores a compounding "debt spiral" where rising interest obligations and persistent government spending create a feedback loop that challenges long-term fiscal sustainability. From a macro perspective, this expansion reflects a fundamental reliance on debt-financed growth, raising significant concerns regarding currency debasement and the future capacity of the Treasury to service these obligations without aggressive monetary intervention.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
