/P 248 0 R
/E (The provided visualization delineates the parabolic expansion of Money Market Fund \(MMF\) assets, which have surpassed the $8 trillion threshold by early 2026, creating an unprecedented pool of "dry powder" within the global financial system. This massive influx into MMFs, accelerating notably since the 2022 tightening cycle, indicates that a vast amount of institutional and retail capital is currently parked in cash equivalents to capture high front-end yields while hedging against macro volatility. For a quantitative analyst in the crypto space, this $8T+ balance represents a dormant liquidity catalyst; as interest rates eventually pivot or confidence in sovereign debt continues to erode, this capital is structurally primed to rotate into scarce, non-sovereign assets like Bitcoin. Essentially, the MMF balance serves as the ultimate "sideline" reservoir, where the sheer magnitude of capital waiting to re-enter risk assets suggests a massive potential re-rating for the digital asset market once the opportunity cost of holding fiat begins to rise.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
