/E (The provided fractal analysis illustrates the historical drawdown of the USD following major macro peaks, specifically comparing the 1985 Plaza Accord, the 2002 Dot-Com Bust, and the 2022 peak driven by inflation and aggressive rate hikes. While the 1985 and 2002 cycles witnessed severe double-digit corrections of up to -40% and -28% respectively within 24 months, the current 2022 cycle is tracking a more measured path, currently sitting near the -12% mark within the "Historical Target Zone" of -10% to -22%. For a research analyst, this fractal serves as a critical lead indicator for fiat debasement cycles; the persistence of the drawdown validates the structural decline thesis and confirms that the currency is struggling to regain its previous peak strength amidst the fiscal pressures discussed in your previous reports. The data suggests that as the USD continues its multi-year descent from the 2022 high, the tailwinds for non-sovereign "hard money" assets will likely intensify as the market prices in a permanent loss of dollar purchasing power.)
