/E (The "Bitcoin Mining Cost Floor" chart highlights a quantitative production model where the market price interacts with the fundamental costs of securing the network, specifically identifying the "Miner Stress Zone" between late 2024 and mid-2025 as a major cyclical buy signal. This zone occurs when the Bitcoin market price drops below the total production cost \(OpEx\) while remaining supported by the electrical cost floor, indicating a period of miner capitulation where inefficient operators are flushed out while institutional accumulation historically intensifies. As we progress into early 2026, the clear divergence between the accelerating market price and the steady total production cost signifies a significant expansion in miner profitability and a robust recovery from the previous stress period, confirming the production floor's role as a reliable macro-support level for the asset's long-term valuation.)
