/Title (Q2: What is the "Yield Trap," and how does it trigger a massive capital rotation into the crypto market? Answer: The Yield Trap occurs when interest rates stay high enough to keep trillions of dollars \(currently $8T+\) parked in Money Market Funds \(MMFs\). However, once the Fed Funds Rate drops below the "Institutional Hurdle Rate" \(around 3.65%\), the opportunity cost of holding cash becomes too high. This "breaks" the trap, forcing institutional capital to rotate into risk-on assets like Bitcoin to maintain their 5.0% alpha targets.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 962 0 R
/Prev 1156 0 R
/Next 1272 0 R
>>
endobj
