/Title (Q3: Why is the divergence between the DXY and the TWI called a "Macro Illusion"? Answer: The DXY is heavily weighted toward the Euro \(57.6%\), making it a poor representation of global dollar strength. If the DXY falls while the Trade-Weighted Index \(TWI\) remains high, it creates an illusion of liquidity expansion. For traders, this is a warning: the "dollar wrecking ball" is still active in the real global economy, even if the headline DXY suggests a bullish environment for risk assets.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 962 0 R
/Prev 1261 0 R
/Next 1262 0 R
>>
endobj
