/Title (The "Rotation Trigger" chart illustrates the widening spread between the 5.0% Equity Earnings Yield and the declining Money Market Fund \(MMF\) Yield, which is projected to drop toward the 3.4% level by late 2026. This expanding "Incentive to Rotate" \(Alpha\) shaded area represents the increasing opportunity cost of holding cash equivalents as the risk-free rate falls, structurally forcing institutional capital out of the $8T+ MMF reservoir and into risk-on assets. For a macro-focused researcher, this trend signals a critical shift where capital seeks higher-beta performance to compensate for the diminishing returns of fiat-based cash. This "yield trap" break historically precedes significant liquidity inflows into equities and high-conviction non-sovereign assets like Bitcoin, as investors pivot to capture the widening yield premium.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1154 0 R
/Prev 1286 0 R
/Next 1289 0 R
>>
endobj
